UID:82b36023fe3a3fba@nutcracker2026
DTSTAMP:20260914T010516Z
SEQUENCE:2026091401
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T205000
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Cast A (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Wed. Dec. 9 · Call 7:30 PM · 8:10 PM–8:50 PM · Robinson 
 Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 7:30 PM: dancers must b
 e checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 7:15 PM. BA: Call Time
  is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minute
 s before Call Time.\nACT II Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair a
 nd Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named. SUBJECT TO CHAN
 GE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal a
 re the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1
 xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP 
 for Coffee: Arabian Coffee — Costume (you provide): Flesh-tone Camisol
 e Leotard\, No tights\; Shoes: Flesh-tone Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Full St
 age Makeup - Mascara Only OK\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\nFull Stage Make
 up Instruction Sheet:\n•  Apply foundation and powder matching skin
 tone\n•  Light skin tone eye shadow over entire eye\n•  Dark b
 rown eye shadow over crease\n•  Medium brown eye shadow blended ove
 r brown\n•  Black fake eyelashes (note: apply mascara to own lashes
  before application of fake lashes)\n•  Apply eyeliner after lashes
  dry\n•  Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doe
 sn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n•  Brown or tan on con
 tour cheekbones\, hairline\n•  Use a brow pencil (or eyeshadow) to 
 darken the eyebrows\n•  Red or Dark Red Lipstick\nDancers of Color 
 may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Gu
 idelines:\n•  Handle costume pieces with care while changing to pre
 vent damage to delicate fabrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas
  in the event of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter ho
 w significant\n•  Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\
 , or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting
  on the floor while in costume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\,
  clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n•  Never apply stage 
 make-up while in costume and shall take great care to refrain from smudg
 ing make-up on costume during its removal\n•  Refrain from the use 
 of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n•  Never wear any gar
 ment not assigned to cast member\n•  Do not handle or consume food 
 or beverage while in costume\, with the exception of water\n•  Do n
 ot remove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theate
 r\n•  Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs fol
 lowing their use\n•  Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n
 •  Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ ward
 robe policies\n•  Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or 
 anything that may damage or stain costumes.
