DESCRIPTION:Wed. Dec. 9 · 9:00 PM–9:30 PM · Robinson Center\nMANDATOR
 Y — production week. BA: Call Time is the time dancers should be check
 -in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Time.\nIn Performance 
 Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named
 . SUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails an
 d the BA portal are the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com
 /spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME
  / HAIR / MAKEUP for Coffee: Arabian Coffee — Costume (you provide): F
 lesh-tone Camisole Leotard\, No tights\; Shoes: Flesh-tone Ballet Shoes\
 ; Makeup: Full Stage Makeup - Mascara Only OK\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part
 \nFull Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n•  Apply foundation and pow
 der matching skintone\n•  Light skin tone eye shadow over entire ey
 e\n•  Dark brown eye shadow over crease\n•  Medium brown eye s
 hadow blended over brown\n•  Black fake eyelashes (note: apply masc
 ara to own lashes before application of fake lashes)\n•  Apply eyel
 iner after lashes dry\n•  Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply ple
 nty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n•  Br
 own or tan on contour cheekbones\, hairline\n•  Use a brow pencil (
 or eyeshadow) to darken the eyebrows\n•  Red or Dark Red Lipstick\n
 Dancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.
 \nCostume Care Guidelines:\n•  Handle costume pieces with care whil
 e changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n•  Promptly notif
 y Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at the point of discove
 ry\, no matter how significant\n•  Never throw costumes or accessor
 ies on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n•  Ref
 rain from sitting on the floor while in costume\n•  Do not attempt 
 to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n•  N
 ever apply stage make-up while in costume and shall take great care to r
 efrain from smudging make-up on costume during its removal\n•  Refr
 ain from the use of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n•  N
 ever wear any garment not assigned to cast member\n•  Do not handle
  or consume food or beverage while in costume\, with the exception of wa
 ter\n•  Do not remove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms o
 r from the theater\n•  Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pi
 eces and wigs following their use\n•  Return all headpieces to thei
 r assigned bags\n•  Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet
  Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n•  Do not pack markers\, paints\, c
 olored drinks or anything that may damage or stain costumes.
